---
import { ClientRouter } from 'astro:transitions';
import HallSession from '../components/hall/HallSession.astro';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<ClientRouter fallback="swap" /><HallSession /><script is:inline src="/nexus/main.js" defer></script>
<meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>NEXUS Library — All your games. Your own universe.</title>
<meta name="description" content="A personal Windows game library. Bring your launchers together, switch between six views, and make your collection feel like yours. Download NEXUS Library.">
<meta name="theme-color" content="#090b12"><link rel="canonical" href="https://www.dennisbf.design/nexus/"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:title" content="NEXUS Library — All your games. Your own universe."><meta property="og:description" content="A personal Windows game library. Bring your launchers together, switch between six views, and make your collection feel like yours. Download NEXUS Library."><meta property="og:url" content="https://www.dennisbf.design/nexus/"><meta property="og:image" content="https://www.dennisbf.design/nexus/assets/home.webp">
<link rel="icon" href="/nexus/assets/nexus.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
<link rel="preload" href="/nexus/assets/outfit.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/nexus/styles.css">
</head>
<body>
<a href="#main" class="skip">Skip to content</a>
<header class="nav wrap"><a href="#" class="brand" aria-label="Nexus home"><img src="/nexus/assets/nexus-static.svg" alt="" width="42" height="42"><span>NEXUS<small>LIBRARY</small></span></a><nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="#library">Explore</a><a href="#personal">Make it yours</a><a href="#download" class="nav-cta">Download <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></nav></header>
<main id="main">
<section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="title"><div class="hero-intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">YOUR PERSONAL PC GAME LIBRARY</p><h1 id="title">All your games.<br><span>Your own universe.</span></h1></div><div class="hero-aside"><p>Less launcher hopping.<br>More finding your next favorite.</p><a class="button primary download" href="https://github.com/reioken/nexus-releases/releases/latest/download/NEXUS-Library-Setup.exe"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3v12m-5-5 5 5 5-5M5 16v5h14v-5"/></svg>Download for Windows</a><p class="meta">Free · Windows 10 / 11 · 64-bit</p></div></div>
<figure class="hero-screen"><button class="image-open" data-full="home" aria-label="Enlarge Nexus Home screenshot"><img src="/nexus/assets/home.webp" width="2000" height="1190" fetchpriority="high" alt="Nexus Home with Luna Abyss featured above a row of real games"></button><figcaption><span>A HOME FOR YOUR WHOLE COLLECTION</span><span>Steam · Epic · GOG · Riot · Battle.net · Local games</span></figcaption></figure>
<div class="facts"><p><strong>6</strong><span>ways to see your library</span></p><p><strong>22</strong><span>navigation designs</span></p><p><strong>0</strong><span>NEXUS accounts needed</span></p></div>
</section>
<section id="library" class="library wrap" aria-labelledby="library-title"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 / YOUR COLLECTION</p><h2 id="library-title">Find the game.<br>Feel the pull.</h2></div><p>From a wall of covers to the details that help you choose. Give every part of your collection its place.</p></div>
<div class="view-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Library previews"><button id="tab-library" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="preview-library" data-view="library">The library</button><button id="tab-coverflow" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="preview-coverflow" tabindex="-1" data-view="coverflow">Cover Flow</button><button id="tab-details" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="preview-details" tabindex="-1" data-view="details">Game details</button><button id="tab-couch" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="preview-couch" tabindex="-1" data-view="couch">Couch mode</button></div>
<div class="preview-stack">
<section id="preview-library" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-library"><button class="image-open" data-full="library" aria-label="Enlarge library screenshot"><img src="/nexus/assets/library.webp" width="2000" height="1190" loading="lazy" alt="Nexus cover grid showing a collection of games"></button><p>Filter by source, build collections, and keep track of what you want to play next.</p></section>
<section id="preview-coverflow" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-coverflow" hidden><button class="image-open" data-full="coverflow" aria-label="Enlarge Cover Flow screenshot"><img src="/nexus/assets/coverflow.webp" width="2000" height="1190" loading="lazy" alt="Nexus Cover Flow view with game covers arranged in a three-dimensional carousel"></button><p>Browse one cover at a time, with the rest of your collection just a step away.</p></section>
<section id="preview-details" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-details" hidden><button class="image-open" data-full="details" aria-label="Enlarge game details screenshot"><img src="/nexus/assets/details.webp" width="2000" height="1190" loading="lazy" alt="Nexus game details with artwork, progress and game information"></button><p>Artwork, progress, metadata and useful links, together when you need a closer look.</p></section>
<section id="preview-couch" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-couch" hidden><button class="image-open" data-full="couch" aria-label="Enlarge couch mode screenshot"><img src="/nexus/assets/couch.webp" width="2000" height="1190" loading="lazy" alt="Nexus full-screen couch view with large artwork and controller-friendly navigation"></button><p>A bigger view for your controller, your sofa, and a little distance from your desk.</p></section>
</div>
</section>
<section id="personal" class="personal" aria-labelledby="personal-title"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / SET YOUR ATMOSPHERE</p><h2 id="personal-title">Make it feel<br><span>like yours.</span></h2></div><p>Quiet and minimal, bright and open, or a little more electric. Choose a navigation design, tune your colors, and arrange your Home.</p></div><div class="theme-pair"><figure><button class="image-open" data-full="themes" aria-label="Enlarge Aurora design screenshot"><img src="/nexus/assets/themes.webp" width="2000" height="1190" loading="lazy" alt="Nexus library with the colorful Aurora navigation design"></button><figcaption><span>AURORA</span><span>A little more electric.</span></figcaption></figure><figure><button class="image-open" data-full="custom" aria-label="Enlarge design editor screenshot"><img src="/nexus/assets/custom.webp" width="2000" height="1190" loading="lazy" alt="Nexus navigation design gallery showing preset styles and a custom theme"></button><figcaption><span>YOUR DESIGN</span><span>Start with a preset. Make it yours.</span></figcaption></figure></div></div></section>
<section id="download" class="download-section wrap" aria-labelledby="download-title"><div class="download-panel"><img class="download-mark" src="/nexus/assets/nexus-static.svg" width="100" height="100" alt=""><p class="eyebrow">THE NEXT GAME IS ALREADY IN YOUR LIBRARY.</p><h2 id="download-title">Give it a new home.</h2><a class="button primary download" href="https://github.com/reioken/nexus-releases/releases/latest/download/NEXUS-Library-Setup.exe"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3v12m-5-5 5 5 5-5M5 16v5h14v-5"/></svg>Download NEXUS Library</a><p class="meta">Latest release · Windows 10 / 11 · 64-bit</p><p class="download-note">Early access. The installer is currently unsigned, so Windows may show a publisher warning.</p></div>
<div class="faq"><details><summary>Do I still need my other launchers?</summary><p>Yes. NEXUS organizes and launches your games. Store clients, game ownership and their sign-ins are still required where the game needs them.</p></details><details><summary>How do my games get into NEXUS?</summary><p>NEXUS detects installed games and local libraries. For a more complete Steam collection, you can connect your Steam profile and API key. Uninstalled Epic and GOG games can be added through a library-file import.</p></details><details><summary>Do I need another account?</summary><p>No NEXUS account is needed. Your library and preferences are stored on your PC. Extra services such as cover search, deals and live streams may need their own credentials and internet access.</p></details><details><summary>How do updates work?</summary><p>With automatic update checks enabled, NEXUS checks for new releases at startup and downloads available updates. You can review the update controls in Settings. This download link always points to the latest published installer. Older versions with a broken update connection need one manual installation of the current release.</p></details></div>
<p class="capture-note">Screenshots show a populated sample library, including demonstration statistics. Games are not included. Game artwork and trademarks belong to their respective owners.</p>
</section>
</main>
<footer class="footer wrap"><a class="brand" href="#"><img src="/nexus/assets/nexus-static.svg" width="28" height="28" alt=""><span>NEXUS</span></a><p>A personal project by <a href="/" data-astro-reload>Dennis Bierreth Fernandez</a></p><a href="/work/nexus/" data-astro-reload>Behind the project ↗</a></footer>
<dialog id="lightbox" aria-label="Expanded app screenshot"><button class="close" aria-label="Close screenshot">×</button><img alt=""></dialog>
</body></html>



